WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.830
Based on the series of popular Saturday Night
Live sketches about metalhead Wayne Campbell

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:10.760
and his shy best friend Garth, 1992's Wayne's
World was a smash hit and a cultural phenomenon.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.339
It spawned catchphrases galore ...

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:13.639
"Schwing.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:14.740
Schwing."

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.300
... and put Queen's "Bohemian Rhapsody" back
on the pop charts.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.030
The respectable Wayne's World 2 was released
in 1993… and that was just about it from

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:24.070
Wayne and Garth.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.900
Will there ever be a Wayne's World 3?

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.760
Here's an "extreme close-up" on why it'll
never happen.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.860
Get the net!

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:31.260
Sequel slump

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:36.340
Paramount Pictures, the studio behind Wayne's
World, presumably lost a lot of interest in

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:40.070
a third installment after taking a look at
the box office receipts for Wayne's World

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:40.570
2.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:45.220
While it certainly has its funny and memorable
moments, it didn't quite capture the magic

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.020
of the original.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:50.100
Critics thought it was fine, but not as good
as the first Wayne's World… and it only

00:00:50.101 --> 00:00:56.120
made $47 million at the domestic box office,
which was far less impressive than the original's

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.000
$121 million take.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:00.080
"No stairway.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.240
Denied."

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.680
It all added up to a lack of evident demand
for Wayne's World 3, and Hollywood wasn't

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.180
going to put up the tens of millions of dollars
required to make it happen.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.020
Sister slowdowns

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.159
After the phenomenal success of Wayne's World,
a slew of full-length movies based on Saturday

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:18.630
Night Live sketches and characters were released.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:22.670
And not one of them managed to come anywhere
near the box office bucks the first Wayne's

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:23.280
World earned.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:30.900
Coneheads, It's Pat, Stuart Saves His Family,
Blues Brothers 2000, A Night at the Roxbury,

00:01:30.909 --> 00:01:37.719
Superstar, and The Ladies Man were all SNL-inspired
duds that made a combined total of $111 million

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:40.800
in theaters—less than Wayne's World amassed
by itself.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:46.759
The sub-genre died until 2010, when Will Forte's
MacGyver send-up MacGruber hit theaters…and

00:01:46.759 --> 00:01:47.759
bombed.

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:52.279
So, overall, there just hasn't been much of
a demand for movies based on sketches people

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:55.440
can watch at home for free, and that includes
more Wayne's World.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:56.880
Getting busy

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:01.439
The late '90s or early '00s would've been
the right time to strike quickly with another

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:06.249
Wayne's World movie, but Mike Myers was simply
too busy with other projects.

00:02:06.249 --> 00:02:10.399
After Wayne's World 2, Myers regrouped and
came up with another over-the-top, irresistible

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:16.100
character: Austin Powers, a British spy straight
out of a candy-colored '60s British spy movie.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.160
"Yeah, baby, yeah!"

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.739
The first movie in the series, Austin Powers:
International Man of Mystery, was a modest

00:02:23.739 --> 00:02:29.409
hit, but built up such a huge home video following
that the 1999 sequel Austin Powers: The Spy

00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:33.150
Who Shagged Me made more than $200 million
at the box office.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:38.000
The third movie, 2002's Austin Powers in Goldmember,
did even better.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.420
Making those movies, along with voicing the
main character in the Shrek series and taking

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:47.519
roles in films like 54 and Mystery, Alaska,
didn't leave a lot of time for Myers to do

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.320
much else.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:49.840
Family feud

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:54.500
The success of Austin Powers can be partially
blamed for why there was never a third Wayne's

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.280
World movie.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:00.650
The character of Dr. Evil parodied several
James Bond villains, particularly the similar-looking

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.840
Blofeld of You Only Live Twice.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:08.010
But his clipped speaking voice, distant demeanor,
and some physical mannerisms—including extending

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:12.909
his pinky finger while talking—may have
also been inspired by Dana Carvey's around-the-studio

00:03:12.909 --> 00:03:15.879
impression of their old SNL boss, Lorne Michaels.

00:03:15.879 --> 00:03:20.219
"That thing, and then when I saw Mike do it
I did kind of go mmmm."

00:03:20.219 --> 00:03:24.489
That, along with other issues, drove a wedge
between the two actors, who didn't speak for

00:03:24.489 --> 00:03:26.220
years as a result of their tiff.

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:31.340
Happily, they've since made up and have appeared
at Wayne's World screenings and on SNL together.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:32.840
Health matters

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.380
Carvey wasn't physically available to make
Wayne's World 3 when it would've most logically

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.629
entered production, sometime in the mid-to-late-'90s.

00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:44.750
Nor was he able to do much work at all—he
had some major health problems.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:48.980
Experiencing chest pains, Carvey went to a
doctor, where it was discovered that blood

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:50.659
wasn't properly flowing to his heart.

00:03:50.659 --> 00:03:52.719
"Hey, come here, come here, look at this x-ray.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.240
Your heart looks like a pig's a------ look
at that thing.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.220
Carvey underwent several operations to correct
the disorder, including a botched operation

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:04.360
where his doctor fixed the wrong artery, but
has since made a full recovery.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.020
Not interested

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:10.450
Probably the biggest reason why Wayne's World
3 has never happened is that Mike Myers doesn't

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.980
seem to want to do it all that much.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:18.230
In 2008, Myers and Dana Carvey appeared as
Wayne and Garth at the MTV Movie Awards, leaving

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:22.570
many fans to wonder if a third big-screen
outing was in the offing, but Myers said he

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:25.720
did it mainly to get "caught up" with his
old friend Carvey.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:30.470
Three years later, Carvey hosted Saturday
Night Live and brought in Myers for a "Wayne's

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:30.970
World" sketch.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:35.940
That reportedly sparked something in Myers,
because in 2012 sources reported that he'd

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:38.220
written a screenplay for Wayne's World 3.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:43.280
But Myers' team sent out a notice to refute
it all, claiming he hadn't completed a script…nor

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.560
was he even working on one.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.160
Myers and Carvey played Wayne and Garth again
for the SNL 40 special in 2015—and once

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:52.740
again, it sparked movie rumors that Myers
good-naturedly shrugged off.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.840
When asked by The Canadian Press if there
were more Wayne's World films in the future,

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.980
he said he was open to the idea, but that
we shouldn't hold our breath, explaining,

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:04.160
"It would be an interesting examination of
Wayne at 50.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:07.880
I don't know what it would look like, but
the idea of it makes me laugh and Dana and

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:11.180
I had a blast at the 40th anniversary, so
I don't know."

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:13.580
"We're not worthy!

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.110
We're not worthy!"

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:16.640
Thanks for watching!

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.420
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:22.030
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

